.TH MMAP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mmap \- create a memory mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B void* mmap(void* address, size_t byte_count, int protection,
.B            int flags, int descriptor, off_t offset);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a Linux mapping using PROT_* and MAP_* flags.
Pass descriptor \-1 for an anonymous mapping. File offsets must be page aligned.
Use map_failed to check the returned sentinel.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the mapped address, or the Linux MAP_FAILED sentinel (a pointer value
of \-1) with errno set. The header does not define a MAP_FAILED macro; use
map_failed to test the result.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR map_failed (3crunch),
.BR munmap (3crunch),
.BR mmap (2)
